USOS 3.1.2-usos8 patch 9/9 (2026-10-15): APM power-off ACPI mode first, helper ResetSystem last, CMOS breadcrumbs

Windows 98 SE on the ASRock X470 (CSM off, CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos7) stays on
the "shutting down" logo forever. Before usos7 (no APM power-off from the
protected-mode interfaces) it ended at "It's now safe to turn off your
computer". usos7 asks the helper core for UEFI ResetSystem first, then
writes S5 in legacy mode; something in that sequence never returns on the
X470, and nothing records which step it was (no serial port on the board).

Own code from the APM 1.2 and ACPI specifications (ACPI 6.x: 4.8.3.1 PM1
event registers, 4.8.3.2 PM1 control, 5.2.9 FADT, 16.1.6 entering a
sleeping state) and the MC146818 RTC register map:
- apm.c: new order for 5307h BX=0001h CX=0003h from every interface:
  1. SCI_EN = 0 and an SMI_CMD port: FADT ACPI_ENABLE to SMI_CMD, SCI_EN
     polled for at most 1 s; 2. PM1a_EVT and GPE0 status bits cleared, all
     their enables 0; 3. S5 (SLP_TYP from \_S5, PM1a/PM1b, SLP_EN last),
     2 s wait; 4. still on, INT 15h and 32-bit PM only: helper-core
     ResetSystem (2 s timeout) as the last resort; 5. still on: AH=60h.
  Every wait loop is bounded by the PM timer and by a spin count, so a PM
  timer that does not tick cannot turn a wait into a hang.
- Breadcrumbs in battery-backed CMOS, the RTC alarm bytes 01h/03h/05h
  (outside the checksum range; the alarm interrupt stays off). Every value
  is a valid alarm time in the RTC's format (Status B DM, BCD or binary),
  because edk2 PcRtcInit (and firmware derived from it) resets an invalid
  alarm to 00:00:00 at every boot: seconds = 40 + last step, minutes =
  path * 15 + 5307h off call count, hours = 1 + bitmap of the APM
  functions seen (32-bit PM connect, real/16-bit connect, other runtime
  calls). Armed (40/0/1) when CSMWrap starts SeaBIOS (handle_csm_0002);
  every step also goes to port 80h as A0h | step. Own port I/O with
  interrupts off around each index/data pair (hw/rtc.c is not linked into
  the 32-bit segmented code of the 32-bit PM entry). The USOS UEFI menu
  reads them on the next boot of the stick (EFI\USOS\Logs\apm-off.txt).
- biostables.c: PM1a_EVT_BLK / GPE0_BLK and their lengths from the FADT
  (X_ GAS fallbacks) for step 2.
- "USOS APMOFF:" serial lines: path=s5 for the S5 write (all paths),
  path=uefi for the helper step.

Applies on top of patches 0001-0008 to CSMWrap 3.1.2 (808ac8e) with its
seabios submodule (578d260b), patch -p1 from the top of the tree. Part of
CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos8, a MODIFIED version made by the USOS project
(LGPL-2.1 / SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

